<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diogo Gomes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1420–c. 1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diogo Gomes was a Portuguese navigator and explorer in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Prince Henry the Navigator</a>. Around 1456 he sailed far up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-gambia">Gambia</a> River to the market of Cantor, in the kingdom of Kantora, where he learned of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-trade">gold trade</a> of the interior. He later claimed a part in the discovery of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-verde">Cape Verde</a> Islands, and his account of his voyages survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diogo-gomes.jpg" alt="Diogo Gomes" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CorreiaPM · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DiogoGomes.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
